{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790613926,"nonce":"+geG/zd7n75H/6Q8VgvlNu8drFI=","message":"Rescoped 2026-09-28: no hook and no gh poll. Moving the status by itself when a PR opens or merges is an automation rule, which is out of scope (47b8430, 483dbe2; 3df330f named this ticket as the one hardcoded instance). `flow pr [ID]` does all of it when it is run: finds the PR for the current branch with `gh`, attaches it to the issue (ID, or the issue the branch was picked for), and sets the status from the PR state it reads: open -\u003e in-review, merged -\u003e done, otherwise unchanged. It is idempotent, so an agent runs it after `gh pr create` and again after merge, and anyone who wants it automatic calls it from their own cron or CI.","files":null}]}